    "window_tokens": 65,
    "_comment": "Only the six 'hybrid' entries of layers_block_type hold a KV cache; the 32 Mamba layers keep a constant SSM state instead. The state is conv_state (d_conv-1)*conv_dim = 3*4352 plus ssm_state n_mamba_heads*mamba_headdim*mamba_d_state = 64*64*128 = 524288 elements, i.e. 537344 elements = 1.07 MB per sequence -- the same size in every step. At 2*kv_dim*kv_fp = 2*4096*2 = 16 KB per KV token-slot that is 65 token-equivalents, so window_tokens=65 models the state as a constant that does not grow with the prompt. CAVEAT: because those six layers are multi-head (kv_dim 4096, four times Qwen3-8B's GQA width), the per-prompt saving over a full-attention model is 0.85x, not the 0.17x the layer count alone suggests -- see docs/混合注意力模型profile.md."
  }
